<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20102" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hadrūmētum</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Adrūm-</span></b> ), i,
			n. (also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hadrumetus</span></b> ,
			i, f., <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap.
			6, § 670</span></i>), = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἁδρούμητος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city of</i> Africa propria, <i>the
				capital of the province</i> Byzacene, <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 7,
			2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 4, 3, § 25</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Caes. B. C.
				2, 23</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 30,
			29</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Deriv. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hadrūmētīnus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Adr-</span></b> ), a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Hadrumetum</i>, <i>Hadrumetine</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Clodius Albinus,</span>”
				<i>of Hadrumetum</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Capitol. Albin. 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">navis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Act. 27, 2</span></i>
			.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hadrūmētī-ni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m.
			plur., <i>the inhabitants of
				Hadrumetum</i>, <i>Hadrumetines</i>, Auct. B.
			Afr. 97, 2.</div>
